PHOTO-009 (geometry tools for Photo Editor) is implemented on branch
feat/PHOTO-009-geometry-tools — check `gh pr list` before assuming it's
merged.

What it added, and what's worth knowing before touching this area:
- geometry.ts turns every tool into one step of a fixed chain —
  quarter turns → flip → keystone → straighten → free rotate → crop → resize
  — and composes their inverse maps into a single 3×3 matrix (output pixel →
  source pixel). The renderer, the crop overlay, the histogram and the
  Canvas port-back all read that one plan; nothing else knows the order.
- Geometry lives in PhotoAdjustments (`adjustments.geometry`), so undo/redo
  and the `edits` metadata stored on port-back cover it with no second
  history. Crop mode and the locked crop ratio are store state but NOT in
  history.
- warp.ts: affine plans draw through the canvas transform (fast, GPU);
  only a keystone plan goes through the per-pixel homography warp, which
  pre-scales the source to the render's density first.
- The 90° and flip buttons act on the *displayed* image: they remap the
  crop, keystone, straighten and rotate so the same content stays framed.
  usePhotoEditorStore.test.ts has invariance tests for exactly this — any
  new display-space field needs the same treatment in rotate90/flip.
- Port-back (projectSlice.portBackFromPhotoEditor) now takes an optional
  `placement`. With it, the Canvas object is re-placed so the kept content
  stays where it was on the page at the same density (a crop shrinks the
  object, a resample keeps its size), and any Canvas-side crop window is
  dropped. Without it (untouched geometry) nothing about the object moves,
  exactly as before.
- A JPEG source rotated by a non-right angle is saved as PNG so the
  uncovered corners stay clear.

Known limitations, deliberate:
- The crop is stored as fractions of the post-rotation frame, so moving
  straighten/rotate/keystone *after* cropping shifts the framed content a
  little (free rotate grows the frame, so the crop grows with it). The 90°
  and flip buttons are exact. Worth a ticket if it bites.
- Perspective is keystone (vertical + horizontal sliders), not free
  four-corner dragging.
- Pre-existing, not from this ticket: fabric logs "ctx"/"clearRect" page
  errors when switching between Canvas and Photo Editor (CanvasStage
  dispose); reproducible on main with no Photo Editor edits.

